***************************** T A L Y S **************************3028 1451  177
                                                                  3028 1451  178
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   3028 1451  179
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      3028 1451  180
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    3028 1451  181
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     3028 1451  182
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  3028 1451  183
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        3028 1451  184
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    3028 1451  185
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         3028 1451  186
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      3028 1451  187
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    3028 1451  188
stored in this data file:                                         3028 1451  189
                                                                  3028 1451  190
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   3028 1451  191
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     3028 1451  192
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 3028 1451  193
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   3028 1451  194
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                3028 1451  195
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   3028 1451  196
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    3028 1451  197
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        3028 1451  198
- Recoil data                                                     3028 1451  199
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           3028 1451  200
- Total particle energy spectra                                   3028 1451  201
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      3028 1451  202
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        3028 1451  203
- Residual production cross sections                              3028 1451  204
                                                                  3028 1451  205
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            3028 1451  206
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        3028 1451  207
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   3028 1451  208
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                3028 1451  209
                                                                  3028 1451  210
